   789	## Wave 016 — Canvas presentation read ports and overlay interaction boundary
   790	
   791	**Scope**
   792	
   793	- `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasPresentationController.ts`
   794	- `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasPresentationSelector.ts`
   795	- `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasPresentationModel.ts`
   796	- `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasInteractionQuery.ts`
   797	- `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasVisibilityPolicy.ts`
   798	- `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasStylePolicy.ts`
   799	- a new narrow canvas presentation read-port module such as `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/CanvasWorldReadPort.ts`
   800	- a named projected-3D-on-2D adapter such as `frontend/src/application/canvasPresentation/Projected3DCanvasSelector.ts`
   801	- `frontend/src/application/threePresentation/*` only where shared overlay/projection DTO ownership is needed
   802	- `frontend/src/rendering/threeView/*` only where explicit pointer-event/overlay boundary behavior is needed
   803	- `frontend/src/components/workspace/SvgCanvas.vue`
   804	- `frontend/src/components/panels/ThreeView.vue`
   805	- `frontend/src/domain/presentation/Paper.ts` only if static usage proves its mutable query responsibilities are obsolete
   806	- focused unit tests under current canvas/three presentation test locations and current-contract e2e/live checks if overlay behavior changes
   807	
   808	**Scope guard**
   809	
   810	This wave replaces the now-invalid old Wave 007/008/009 premises rather than continuing them literally. The old Wave 007 named `PaperService.ts` and `RenderService.ts`, but current scout evidence says those files are absent and the active rendering path is `SVGRenderer.ts` plus `canvasPresentation/*`. The old Wave 008 assumed a large `ThreeView.vue` extraction, but current `ThreeView.vue` is already a small runtime shell. The old Wave 009 app-shell god-component premise is also mostly invalidated by the current `App.vue` runtime/action composition. Therefore this wave is the next central post-Wave-015 source boundary: active canvas presentation still receives full `World`, contains `any` seams, embeds projected-3D-on-2D ownership, and has user-observable overlay pointer interception that validation previously routed around.
   811	
   812	Do not reopen broad rendering, 3D scene, app-shell, command, persistence, backend, package/tooling, docs/spec, or validation-platform redesigns inside this wave. If implementation discovers those areas are required, stop and run a reviewed plan-edit mini-cycle before broadening scope.
   813	
   814	**Target outcome**
   815	
   816	The 2D canvas presentation path consumes explicit narrow read ports/DTOs instead of a full mutable `World`; 2D primitive selection, projected-3D-on-2D projection, hit/query input, style policy, visibility policy, and overlay event ownership have named modules with one responsibility each. Broad `any` helper seams in active presentation code are deleted rather than cast over. The 3D overlay either deliberately owns pointer interaction in its region or deliberately allows underlying canvas interaction; that contract is encoded in source and tests instead of hidden in e2e click-coordinate workarounds.
   817	
   818	**Explicit DELETE list**
   819	
   820	- Delete `CanvasPresentationController.buildModel(world: World, ...)` or any equivalent full-`World` selector API once the reviewed read port is introduced.
   821	- Delete `CanvasPresentationSelector` helper signatures that use `any`, including untyped primitive/kind and plane-transform helper seams.
   822	- Delete direct projected-3D rendering loops from `CanvasPresentationSelector` when moved to a named projected-3D canvas selector/adapter.
   823	- Delete obsolete selector tests that instantiate concrete `World` only to inspect traversal internals; replace them with read-port/DTO tests.
   824	- Delete mutable/spatial-query responsibilities from `frontend/src/domain/presentation/Paper.ts` only if static usage and focused tests prove `CanvasInteractionQuery` is the active query owner.
   825	- Delete e2e workarounds that avoid overlay interception if the implementation changes overlay input ownership; replace them with current behavior contracts.
   826	- Delete any compatibility wrapper, dual full-`World`/read-port path, broad presentation facade, or dead export created during the transition.
   827	
   828	**Success criteria**
   829	
   830	- Canvas presentation selectors/controllers no longer depend on a full mutable `World` where a narrow read port/DTO is sufficient.
   831	- Active `CanvasPresentationSelector` helper seams no longer use `any` for primitive/kind or plane-transform data.
   832	- Projected-3D-on-2D rendering has an explicit owner outside the general 2D selector loop, or the implementation log explains with reviewed evidence why the owner remains there.
   833	- Overlay pointer ownership is inventoried against current `ThreeView`/three-rendering handlers before any behavior change, then covered by focused e2e/live evidence if user-observable behavior changes.
   834	- No broad rendering platform, shared god snapshot factory, app-shell redesign, command/persistence/backend change, package/tooling change, or stale audit-history dependency is introduced.
   835	- Mandatory validation cadence passes with stable logs: root/frontend lint where defined, focused Vitest for touched presentation/query modules, full root/frontend Vitest, root/frontend build, root/frontend e2e when user-facing overlay/canvas behavior changes, live preview refresh on `0.0.0.0:5173`, HTTP reachability probe, and Playwright/live browser evidence for the affected canvas/overlay region when applicable.
   836	
   837	**Dependencies**
   838	
   839	Depends on Wave 015 and the subsequent Wave 014 validation closure, because this wave relies on the now-green TypeScript/build/test/e2e gates and on the extracted command/use-case, rendering, and validation contracts produced by earlier cycles. It is ordered before any remaining peripheral docs/debug cleanup because it is the most central current user-input/rendering boundary left after Wave 015.
   840	
   841	**Validation requirements**
   842	
   843	1. Capture static scans for full-`World` canvas presentation APIs, `CanvasPresentationSelector` `any` seams, projected-3D loops, `Paper` query usage, and current 3D overlay pointer handlers before edits.
   844	2. Run focused Vitest for changed canvas presentation selector/controller/read-port/query modules and any three-presentation shared DTO/overlay boundary.
   845	3. Run root and frontend lint where scripts exist.
   846	4. Run full root and frontend Vitest.
   847	5. Run root and frontend build.
   848	6. Run root/frontend Playwright e2e if overlay/canvas interaction or other user-facing behavior changes; otherwise record exact justification in the implementation log.
   849	7. Refresh the live preview on `0.0.0.0:5173`, capture an HTTP 200 reachability probe, and run a Playwright/live browser check for the current canvas area affected by the 3D overlay.
   850	
